<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Frost Mages</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 15%. Keep in mind that some abilities such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-expertise-rating">Hit &amp; Expertise Rating</h4>At 15% Hit, your spells will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. It's also relevant to note that Expertise now counts as Hit and should be added together for the total of 15% to reach said cap.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c8" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Frost Mages</span></h2>As a Frost Mage, Haste is the best secondary stat, and because at the item level of a end-game set 2 Haste is better than 1 Intellect, you start focusing on secondary stat gems more so than Intellect focused gems.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
